  "bounded_source_observations": [
    "The twelve operations change only method selection, explicit method observations, operation/job quantity naming and corresponding author checks/docs/contract. The full main/helper reconstruction and inverse recover immutableV1, so cold reopen, SQL logical durability, source A/archive provenance, complete original64MiB public EOF/hash/tail, +1 incomplete-prefix controls, quota/cursor/corruption/drop checks and failure-only owned cleanup remain as previously read.",
    "Six whole critical regions independently match immutableV1, including genuine64MiB,64MiB+1, selected public full EOF/SHA, natural child/pipe/owner guards, actual HTTP request resource ownership and streamed fixture generation. Admission remains byte-identical, dynamically requires independently reviewed actual Source6 binder plus actual future source/suite/build/candidate proofs and reads only the Root-outer-owned global lock.",
    "Current BinderV2 and future actual Source6 freeze/formatter/suite/build/candidate references must be supplied through the actual Root release. Historical BinderV1 reference files remain source provenance only; no V1 or Source5 PASS is transferred. This review does not issue a runtime release.",
    "No fixture, SQLite, listener, HTTP request, child app, compiler, Rust test, browser or target import was executed. All thirteen acceptance cases remain AUTHORED_NOT_RUN. No universal transport/App deadline, RSS, manufacturer parity or installation claim follows."
